Date: Sun, 5 Jul 2026 15:17:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: interrupt-controller: apple,aic2: Add
 apple,t8132 compatible

The Apple t8132 (M4) SoC uses an AIC3 as interrupt controller, same as
the M3 predecessor.

Signed-off-by: Yureka Lilian <yureka@cyberchaos.dev>
Reviewed-by: Krzysztof Kozlowski <krzysztof.kozlowski@oss.qualcomm.com>
(cherry picked from commit ccbe86a1f99d9f6e2095d8e1867e7ef80ce8bb03)
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/interrupt-controller/apple,aic2.yaml     | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/interrupt-controller/apple,aic2.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/interrupt-controller/apple,aic2.yaml
index 726a6720e05f..1cb886785173 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/interrupt-controller/apple,aic2.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/interrupt-controller/apple,aic2.yaml
@@ -45,6 +45,7 @@ properties:
           - enum:
               - apple,t6030-aic3
               - apple,t6031-aic3
+              - apple,t8132-aic3
           - const: apple,t8122-aic3
       - const: apple,t8122-aic3
 
